WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:17.418
"Oof!" Zann grunted as he and his friends landed on something soft.

2
00:00:17.419 --> 00:00:21.226
"Where are we?" Perda cried. "Help!"

3
00:00:21.227 --> 00:00:24.504
"Hush, children," said a voice from the darkness.

4
00:00:24.505 --> 00:00:28.182
It didn't sound like a troll. But Zann jumped to his feet.

5
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:32.178
"Ouch!" Darb yelped. "Who stepped on my hand?"

6
00:00:32.179 --> 00:00:34.683
"Sorry," Zann said.

7
00:00:34.684 --> 00:00:41.396
A flame flickered to life. Zann squinted, barely making out a human-shaped shadow behind it.

8
00:00:41.397 --> 00:00:44.393
Whoever it was didn't look like a troll either.

9
00:00:44.394 --> 00:00:48.375
"Who's there?" he asked, trying to sound brave.

10
00:00:48.376 --> 00:00:51.230
"Don't be frightened, my young friends."

11
00:00:51.231 --> 00:00:57.272
The torch grew brighter, revealing the person behind the voice: a Red around Boz's age.

12
00:00:57.273 --> 00:01:03.469
His gray-streaked hair stuck up in all directions, as if it were trying to escape from his head.

13
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:07.573
His bright blue eyes were shaded by huge, bushy brows.

14
00:01:07.574 --> 00:01:11.930
"Who are you?" Perda stared at the old man's multicolored robe.

15
00:01:11.931 --> 00:01:16.382
It was a little too short, ending just above his bony ankles.

16
00:01:16.383 --> 00:01:19.944
The man smiled. "My name is Teplo."

17
00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:25.464
Zann gasped. "Teplo? But that woman upstairs said—"

18
00:01:25.465 --> 00:01:32.278
"That's Fala, my assistant." Teplo set the torch in a wall bracket and lit two more.

19
00:01:32.279 --> 00:01:37.231
"She's under strict orders to say I've been taken." He peered at Zann.

20
00:01:37.232 --> 00:01:45.136
"You're Boz's grandson, aren't you? You look just like the blink images I've seen of you. Except older, of course."

21
00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:50.342
"Uh, yeah, I'm Zann. These are my friends Perda and Darb."

22
00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.661
Teplo didn't look anything like Zann had imagined.

23
00:01:53.662 --> 00:01:59.038
He'd been expecting someone more like the king—tall, handsome, and strong.

24
00:01:59.039 --> 00:02:03.337
"Charmed to make your acquaintance." Teplo made an elaborate bow.

25
00:02:03.338 --> 00:02:07.111
"My apologies for the abruptness of your arrival."

26
00:02:07.112 --> 00:02:09.431
Perda glanced around the underground room.

27
00:02:09.432 --> 00:02:12.661
"Did you open a trapdoor to get us down here?"

28
00:02:12.662 --> 00:02:19.184
"I did." Teplo chuckled. "I built the trapdoor years ago as an experiment.

29
00:02:19.185 --> 00:02:23.699
When I heard you mention Boz, I thought perhaps I should use it."

30
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.926
He hurried to a corner of the room and yanked on a rope.

31
00:02:26.927 --> 00:02:31.024
Somewhere overhead the kids heard the muffled sound of a bell ringing.

32
00:02:31.025 --> 00:02:34.059
"Fala will be along soon with food and drink."

33
00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:40.064
Teplo grabbed a bowl from a table. "In the meantime you can snack on these turnip cookies."

34
00:02:40.065 --> 00:02:43.756
Perda wrinkled her nose. "Turnip cookies?"

35
00:02:43.757 --> 00:02:49.610
Zann's stomach grumbled and he realized none of them had eaten that day. He reached for a cookie.

36
00:02:49.611 --> 00:02:55.205
"How'd you dodge the trolls?" he asked Teplo, cautiously nibbling on the cookie.

37
00:02:55.206 --> 00:02:58.433
It tasted like dirt mixed with swamp water.

38
00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:03.550
"It wasn't easy." Teplo held up a cookie, staring at it thoughtfully.

39
00:03:03.551 --> 00:03:08.043
"I had to call upon my old friend the turnip for help."

40
00:03:08.044 --> 00:03:10.959
Zann and his friends traded a glance.

41
00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:16.795
So far Teplo seemed pretty weird, with his crazy clothes and his talk about turnips.

42
00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:22.362
Could he really be the great Magic Master whom Zann had heard stories about all his life?

43
00:03:22.363 --> 00:03:26.126
"Um, the turnip?" Perda said politely.

44
00:03:26.127 --> 00:03:32.166
Teplo nodded. "The turnip comes from another world originally. Did you know that?"

45
00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:34.344
The kids shook their heads.

46
00:03:34.345 --> 00:03:40.933
"It's true." Teplo continued. "That gives it great power if one knows how to harness it."

47
00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:44.976
Zann wasn't interested in wasting time talking about turnips.

48
00:03:44.977 --> 00:03:47.757
They had to find Gliss before it was too late.

49
00:03:47.758 --> 00:03:52.477
"We tried to visit Lonz and Saffa, but they're both gone," he said.

50
00:03:52.478 --> 00:03:56.416
"Unless they're in hiding too?" Perda asked hopefully.

51
00:03:56.417 --> 00:04:01.750
"No, they're gone," Teplo said. "Only a few of us remain free.

52
00:04:01.751 --> 00:04:06.649
Of course none of us can use magic, so it's difficult to keep track."

53
00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:10.976
"I guess you figured out that Morb can track people through their magic?" Darb asked.

54
00:04:10.977 --> 00:04:19.155
"Indeed," said Teplo. "Morb is using a very old form of magic that was banned long ago by the Red Council.

55
00:04:19.156 --> 00:04:22.637
But it's easy to detect if you know what to look for.

56
00:04:22.638 --> 00:04:25.994
Now tell me your story, young friends."

57
00:04:25.995 --> 00:04:30.440
Zann only hesitated for a moment. Yes, Teplo was odd.

58
00:04:30.441 --> 00:04:35.407
But he was Boz's friend and Zann and his friends clearly needed help from someone.

59
00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:40.077
"It all started when an echo crow came to school . . ." Zann began.

60
00:04:40.078 --> 00:04:43.961
With help from the others, he told Teplo the whole story.

61
00:04:43.962 --> 00:04:48.542
The old man listened carefully, not saying a word until they were finished.

62
00:04:48.543 --> 00:04:54.822
"Very interesting," Teplo said then. "Does anyone else know you're in First City?"

63
00:04:54.823 --> 00:04:59.531
"Just Slib and Yog and the others at the palace," Zann said.

64
00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:03.643
"Plus Lonz's daughter and Saffa's husband, I guess.

65
00:05:03.644 --> 00:05:06.176
We didn't tell them who we were though."

66
00:05:06.177 --> 00:05:11.822
"Don't forget that strange old woman we talked to in Wormwood when we first arrived," Darb said.

67
00:05:11.823 --> 00:05:15.629
Zann nodded. Darb was very logical and thorough.

68
00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.377
It figured he'd remember that brief encounter.

69
00:05:18.378 --> 00:05:27.862
Teplo leaned forward. "Wormwood?" he echoed, his blue eyes suddenly sharp with interest. "What old woman?"

70
00:05:27.863 --> 00:05:32.170
"Just some crazy old lady near the big tree," Zann said.

71
00:05:32.171 --> 00:05:35.825
"She wanted to trade us some disguises for Zing."

72
00:05:35.826 --> 00:05:38.653
"That's Zann's pet dragon," Darb explained.

73
00:05:38.654 --> 00:05:40.962
"They took Zing from us at the palace."

74
00:05:40.963 --> 00:05:46.926
Teplo didn't seem to hear him. "Wyssa," he muttered. "This could be trouble."

75
00:05:46.927 --> 00:05:50.163
"Huh?" Zann said. "Who's Wyssa?"

76
00:05:50.164 --> 00:05:53.283
Teplo waved a hand, his eyes calm again.

77
00:05:53.284 --> 00:05:59.333
"Never mind. Talking to myself," he said. "Now where's Fala with our food?"

78
00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:02.050
If the others responded, Zann didn't hear it.

79
00:06:02.051 --> 00:06:05.210
A sudden wave of strong emotion overcame him.

80
00:06:05.211 --> 00:06:08.699
He grabbed the back of a chair to keep from falling down.

81
00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:15.935
Finally he blinked and looked up. The others were staring at him. "A Red Share, huh?" Teplo said.

82
00:06:15.936 --> 00:06:20.023
"Was it from Boz?" Perda asked. "This could be important!

83
00:06:20.024 --> 00:06:25.040
Shares can only be felt if the two people are near each other, so that means—"

84
00:06:25.041 --> 00:06:29.254
"N-no!" Zann stammered. "It wasn't from Boz.

85
00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:38.497
It was from Gliss. And she's really scared!"
